@startuml state_machine_rt
title RT State Machine (per LLR-1553-RT-013)

[*] --> RESET

RESET --> IDLE : PBIT pass
RESET --> FAIL_SAFE : PBIT fail

IDLE --> WAIT_COMMAND : enable

WAIT_COMMAND --> VALIDATE : command word\naddressed to self\nor broadcast (RT-001)

VALIDATE --> EXECUTE : valid command
VALIDATE --> ERROR : transmission error\nor illegal command
VALIDATE --> BUSY : subsystem busy

EXECUTE --> RESPOND

RESPOND --> WAIT_COMMAND : last word sent

ERROR --> WAIT_COMMAND : status word sent\n(or none needed)

BUSY --> RESPOND

RESET --> FAIL_SAFE : fatal BIT result
IDLE --> FAIL_SAFE : fatal BIT result
WAIT_COMMAND --> FAIL_SAFE : fatal BIT result
VALIDATE --> FAIL_SAFE : fatal BIT result
EXECUTE --> FAIL_SAFE : fatal BIT result
RESPOND --> FAIL_SAFE : fatal BIT result
ERROR --> FAIL_SAFE : fatal BIT result
BUSY --> FAIL_SAFE : fatal BIT result

IDLE --> RESET : reset mode command
WAIT_COMMAND --> RESET : reset mode command
VALIDATE --> RESET : reset mode command
EXECUTE --> RESET : reset mode command
RESPOND --> RESET : reset mode command
ERROR --> RESET : reset mode command
BUSY --> RESET : reset mode command
FAIL_SAFE --> RESET : reset mode command

note right of FAIL_SAFE
  In FAIL_SAFE, RT executes no
  command; a command addressed
  to it is answered with a
  status word, TF set, no data
  words (stays visible to BC).
end note

@enduml